n breath tests for diagnosing malabsorption.", "METANO:Methane is another gas produced during fermentation in the colon, which can also be measured in breath tests.", "PREPARACIONES PARA COLONOSCOPIA:Preparaciones para colonoscopia are procedures that can affect the microbiota and should be avoided before breath tests.", "DIETA BAJA EN HC FERMENTABLES:Dieta baja en HC fermentables is a dietary approach recommended before breath tests to ensure accurate results.", "LCT:Long-chain triglycerides (LCT) are fats that play a crucial role in providing essential fatty acids, particularly in infant nutrition. However, they may also have adverse effects on liver function in patients suffering from chronic pancreatitis. Additionally, the LCT gene is significant as it encodes the lactase enzyme, which is essential for the digestion of lactose. This gene is responsible for the production of lactase, enabling the breakdown of lactose in the body. Thus, LCT encompasses both dietary fats important for nutrition and a gene vital for lactose metabolism.", "AFRICA:Africa has a high prevalence of lactose intolerance, ranging from 65-75%.", "ASIA:Asia has the highest prevalence of lactose intolerance, exceeding 90%.", "NATIVE AMERICANS:Native Americans have a very high prevalence of lactose intolerance, estimated at 90-95%.", "HAPLOTYPES:Haplotypes are genetic variations associated with lactase persistence in different populations.", "SNP:Single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) are genetic variations that influence lactase expression and persistence.", "HIPOLACTASIA DEL ADULTO:Hipolactasia del adulto es la causa más frecuente de intolerancia a los hidratos de carbono, típica en niños mayores y adultos.", "PERIODO PERINATAL:El período perinatal es el tiempo alrededor del nacimiento, donde la expresión de lactasa aumenta.", "SÍNDROME DE INTESTINO IRRITABLE:The \"Síndrome de Intestino Irritable\" (Irritable Bowel Syndrome, IBS) is a common gastrointestinal disorder characterized by a range of symptoms including cramping, abdominal pain, bloating, gas, and alterations in bowel habits such as diarrhea or constipation. It is classified as a functional gastrointestinal disorder, meaning that it affects the normal functioning of the digestive system without any identifiable structural abnormalities. Symptoms often worsen after meals and can include abdominal pain and urgency to defecate.\n\nDiagnosis of IBS requires differentiation from other conditions, such as lactose intolerance and celiac disease, as it can exhibit similar symptoms. Additionally, IBS can be influenced by food intolerances and may exacerbate symptoms related to fructose malabsorption. Current research is exploring potential treatments for IBS, including the use of probiotics, to help manage its symptoms effectively."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}